# secrets -- never commit
.env
*.pem
*.key

# runtime data (encrypted blobs + sqlite)
#
# ANCHORED (leading slash) on purpose, and the slash is load-bearing. An unanchored
# `data/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, which also matched
# `secure_context_pipeline/detection/data/` -- the shipped gazetteers `diagnoses.txt`
# and `medications.txt`. `entities.yaml` names both as required gazetteers and
# `load_registry` fails closed without them, so with the unanchored rule a fresh
# `git clone` could not start: `demo.py` exited 2 on
# `ConfigError(reason='registry_gazetteer_missing')` and the suite raised 457 errors.
# It was invisible locally precisely because the files were ignored -- `git status`
# reported clean and every local run worked.
#
# `.dockerignore` keeps the UNANCHORED spelling for the same intent, because Docker's
# matcher anchors at the context root already; see the comment there. The two files
# look inconsistent and must stay that way. Pinned by
# `tests/test_api.py::test_every_runtime_asset_the_registry_needs_actually_reaches_the_image`,
# which now asserts the files are *tracked by git*, not merely present on disk.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# demo artifacts
wire_dump*.txt

# CodeGraph index -- local developer tooling, not part of the submission.
# Anchored for the same reason `/data/` is: an unanchored rule would also match a
# `.codegraph` directory at any depth.
/.codegraph/

# os
.DS_Store

# Tooling state that is per-developer, not per-repo. Both were invisible here for
# reasons that do not travel: `.claude/settings.local.json` was covered only by a
# MACHINE-GLOBAL ignore (~/.config/git/ignore), which a CI checkout or a teammate's
# clone does not have, and `.hypothesis/` only by a .gitignore Hypothesis writes into
# itself. Neither is this repository's decision until it is written here -- and this
# repo runs `git add -A`, so "untracked" is one careless commit away from "tracked".
.claude/
.hypothesis/
.gstack/
